  {
    "udt_error_enum_v0": {
      "doc": "Error codes live at 300+ **on purpose**, for the same reason `vesting` moved\\nto 100+ and `factory` to 200+.\\n\\n`claim` and `withdraw_unclaimed` both reach `token_client.transfer`, and a\\nStellar Asset Contract raises its own `contracterror` codes across 1\\xe2\\x80\\x9313.\\nUnder the old 1..=16 numbering thirteen of the sixteen variants collided\\nwith that range, and the collisions fell on exactly the failures a caller\\nmust tell apart: an underfunded instance traps with SAC `BalanceError = 10`,\\nwhich this ABI decoded as `TokenTransferMismatch` \\xe2\\x80\\x94 an accusation that the\\ntoken short-credited the transfer, when the campaign simply has no money \\xe2\\x80\\x94\\nand SAC `AllowanceError = 9` decoded as `InvalidAmount`.\\n\\n300+ rather than reusing 100+ or 200+: the ranges must stay MUTUALLY\\ndisjoint, not merely clear of the token. RPC and wallet layers surface a\\nrevert as a bare `Error(Contract, #N)` string with no contract attached, so\\nthe number is the only identifier a decoder has \\xe2\\x80\\x94 1\\xe2\\x80\\x9313 the token, 101\\xe2\\x80\\x93122\\n`vesting`, 201\\xe2\\x80\\x93210 `factory`,",
      "lib": "",
      "name": "Error",
      "cases": [
        {
          "doc": "",
          "name": "AlreadyClaimed",
          "value": 301
        },
        {
          "doc": "",
