          "doc": "",
          "name": "token",
          "type_": "address"
        },
        {
          "doc": "Declared distribution size. Equals `\\xce\\xa3 leaf amount` only by the TRUSTED\\nOFF-CHAIN SOLVENCY INVARIANT: the root commits per-leaf `(index, address,\\namount)`, so the instance can verify a single claim's amount via its proof\\nbut cannot sum all leaves (that needs every proof) \\xe2\\x80\\x94 `total` is therefore\\nNOT bound on-chain to the leaf sum. Construction floor-binds it\\n(`total >= recipient_count`) because every valid claim amount is at\\nleast one base unit; the factory funds exactly `total`.\\nOver-declared `total` strands the surplus (sweepable via\\n`withdraw_unclaimed`); under-declared `total` caps payouts at the funded\\nbalance (claims that would cross the declared total are rejected).",
          "name": "total",
          "type_": "i128"
        }
      ]
    }
